{
 "version": 1,
 "_doc": "Skill tiers (WP2, spec 2026-10-25-npc-world-v1-design.md). Same engine and golden node budget at every tier; low tiers add bounded, believable human mistakes (SkilledPilot), never shallow search: wrong trade target (enemy minions only), going face over a better trade, holding a card for later, planning a turn without the opponent's reply (ignoreAoeRisk, per turn), a greedy mulligan (per match) and missing a long lethal (lethalMiss, once per turn, lethals of >= minLethalActions). Typed-mistake chances are per eligible decision; maxValueLoss / softmaxMaxValueLoss in DeckPlanEvaluator units (a 3/3 minion is ~12). Every in-turn proposal is validated by paired same-root continuation searches; maxValueLoss 0 permits only equal-or-better outcomes, including ignoreAoeRisk and lethalMiss. Greedy mulligan remains a separate pregame policy. misorder is not used until the search exposes its plan line. expert and master keep the golden budget (master spans Diamond 5 to early Legend, and the matchmaker is not recalibrated for a ~+100 Elo shift); elite runs the elite+ budget (2026-10-25 research, docs/roadmap/2026-10-25-npc-elite-research.md): about 10x the golden plan search (own beam 25, 9 reply finalists x 14 samples, lethal 4000), ~4.5x the nodes per decision, and a live search budget of up to 45 s per turn (turnSearchSeconds) that stops new search 55 s into the 75 s retail turn (turnWallSeconds, also clamped to a finite turn deadline such as Nozdormu's 15 s). Owner 2026-11-01 (quality over speed within a retail turn): every tier uses the same 45 s / 55 s live guards, so slow devices never truncate a tier's node budget; tiers differ by node budget and mistakes, not by clock. replyBlendScale 1 at expert/master/elite. rating bands are nominal; data/npc/calibration-v1.json is a provisional diagnostic (tiers not separable at <=20 games per edge, see the design spec).",
